{number: 29}
{title: Angels We Have Heard on High}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Angels we have [C] heard on [F] high,
Sweetly singing [C] o'er the [F] plains,
And the mountains [C] in re-[F] ply
Echoing their [C] joyous [F] strains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F] Glo-[Dm]-[Gm]-[C7]-[F]-[Bb]-[C] ria, [F] in ex-[C] celsis [F] De-[C] o!
[F] Glo-[Dm]-[Gm]-[C7]-[F]-[Bb]-[C] ria, [F] in ex-[C] celsis [F] De-[C7]-[F] o!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Shepherds, why this [C] jubi-[F] lee?
Why your joyous [C] strains pro-[F] long?
Say what may the [C] tidings [F] be,
Which inspire your [C] heav'nly [F] song?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Come to Bethlehem, [C] and [F] see
Him whose birth the [C] angels [F] sing;
Come, adore on [C] bended [F] knee
Christ the Lord, the [C] newborn [F] King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[F] See within a [C] manger [F] laid
Jesus, Lord of [C] heav'n and [F] earth!
Mary, Joseph, [C] lend your [F] aid,
With us sing our [C] Savior's [F] birth.
{end_of_verse}
